<h1>Register</h1>
<% if (typeof error !== 'undefined' && error) { %><p class="error-box"><%= error %></p><% } %>
<div class="auth-card">
  <form method="post" action="/register" class="form">
    <label>Username <input name="username" required autocomplete="username"></label>
    <label>Password <input name="password" type="password" required autocomplete="new-password"></label>
    <label>Email <input name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email"></label>
    <!-- VULN (A06, mass assignment): role reaches the INSERT. -->
    <label>Role <input name="role" value="customer"></label>
    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Create account</button>
  </form>
</div>
<p class="auth-alt">The “Role” field is here so the <a href="/faq">mass-assignment lab</a> is obvious. A real form would not have it — the attack then uses a crafted POST.</p>